// W7-06 U1/t, S-1172, S-1183 (§11.5: "枝と … には、状態を持つもの … を書けない（E0811。修正候補は `if~` / `match~` にすることと、
// 状態を持つものを前の `let` に出すこと …）"; S-1183, the provisional reading (1)): a thing with state in a branch of a plain
// `if` or `match` that is itself in a branch of another plain `if` or `match`. The error is one (the innermost branch is
// the place), and it has two candidates. The first, the `~` of the innermost `if` / `match`, makes it evaluate every
// branch of its own, but the thing is still in a branch of the outer one, so the E0811 stays after it (`leaves`, at the
// position in the text after the candidate: the thing moves one column right of the inserted `~`). The candidate is
// shown although it leaves the error: the provisional reading (1) of S-1183 (an open detail); applied again to what
// is left, the candidates stop (the loop of the test `candidates_applied_again_stop` of crates/onsa_cli/tests/cli/lift_candidates.rs). The second, the lift
// into a `let` (§11.5), takes the thing out of both and leaves nothing (the runner's default for a candidate with no
// entry). The `if~` and `match~` of the first candidate are read after W7-06 U2 and U3a. One error per flow (P-01); the
// marker is on the line of the offending construct, and the position in the entries is the start of the thing with
// state (S-392, provisional).

pub flow acc(x: F32 at sample) -> F32 at sample {
  let y = x + prev~(^y)
  y
}

pub flow if_in_an_if(x: F32 at sample, c: Bool at sample) -> F32 at sample {
  if c { if x > 1.0 { acc~(x) } else { 0.0 } } else { 0.0 } //~ E0811
}

pub flow match_in_an_if(x: F32 at sample, k: U32 at sample) -> F32 at sample {
  if x > 0.0 { match k { 0 => prev~(x), _ => 0.0 } } else { 0.0 } //~ E0811
}

pub flow if_in_an_arm(x: F32 at sample, k: U32 at sample) -> F32 at sample {
  match k { 0 => if x > 0.0 { acc~(x) } else { 0.0 }, _ => 0.0 } //~ E0811
}
